insert into public.cpl_memory (slug,kind,title,summary,tags,status,source,verified_by,verified_at,author,event_date) values
('m-collection-s741','milestone','S741''s collection: 52 records','S741 (2026-11-27, the routine''s 06:12Z run): 52 records collected and live (28 passing, 24 named gaps by guarded plans): keys 17, readers 20, piles 15. Display a143061a2ae2 (#3898); #3900 repaired main. Census after the display build: 15,642 of 20,282 pass, 3,996 without, 644 with a named gap. Paid reads about $3.',array['program-requirements','collection','milestone'],'proposed','docs/session_742_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyWillet (S741)','2026-11-27'),
('d-reread-before-rebuilt-plan-s741','decision','Reread the reconciled run before rebuilding a plan on its rows','S741 conductor: Copper Mountain''s degree-floor reconcile 45957316339 re-filed 14710, 14737 and 45594, so plan s741k2''s test failed at that head and a reread would have left its guard matching none. The reread of the reconciled run came first, then s741k2 was rebuilt on those rows for its second and last review round.',array['program-requirements','reread','plans','conductor'],'proposed','docs/session_742_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyWillet (S741)','2026-11-27'),
('d-shared-reader-change-reader-on-fable-s741','decision','A shared reader-code change gets the collection model as its second reader','S741 conductor: a second reader of a shared reader-code change (rule B, window_keeps_tabs, cq_group_ends, keep-better''s rank, OPTION_PART) runs on Fable 5.2, the collection model. Sonnet stays the plan reader; Opus stays for workers that write shared data or change an apply, under Sam''s cost rules of 2026-11-25.',array['program-requirements','readers','models','conductor'],'proposed','docs/session_742_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyWillet (S741)','2026-11-27'),
('d-crc-filing-parked-for-moved-pdf-s741','decision','Cosumnes River''s filing is parked because its PDF repaginated','S741 conductor: Cosumnes River''s free reconcile 45972311864 passed 33542 by OPTION_PART, but the compiled PDF repaginated (Marketing p.474 to p.473), so the fresh capture moves 04596 and 35899 and two S739 tests fail. Parked on claude/s741-keys-crc (49e6c644), reverted on claude/s741-keys; the next session adds either-state test edits, then rereads.',array['program-requirements','cosumnes-river','parked','conductor'],'proposed','docs/session_742_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyWillet (S741)','2026-11-27'),
('p-noncredit-test-injected-key-collides-with-live-save-s741','pitfall','A test that injects a key collides with a person''s live save of it','S741: tests/subject_decisions_noncredit_test.py injected a Los Angeles Pierce OLD noncredit save and assumed it adds one applied decision. The sync carried a person''s save of that key, lints (6) went red on main, and every PR''s test runs on its merge with main. #3900 expects one more only while no live save holds the key.',array['ci','tests','subject-decisions','pitfall'],'proposed','docs/session_742_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyWillet (S741)','2026-11-27'),
('p-conductor-apply-from-detached-head-s741','pitfall','The conductor applies from a detached HEAD, not the worker''s branch name','S741: the conductor''s apply worktree had checked out the worker''s branch name, so its pushes moved the worker''s local ref. The conductor now applies from a detached HEAD and pushes HEAD:<branch>, so a worker''s local ref never moves under it.',array['conductor','apply','git','pitfall'],'proposed','docs/session_742_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyWillet (S741)','2026-11-27'),
('p-migrate-queue-global-pending-cancels-s741','pitfall','The migrate queue is global: a second pending run cancels the first','S741: supabase-migrate.yml''s queue is global, so a second pending run cancels the first. Run one apply at a time and restore .apply after each (s741a, s741b, s741c and s741k2 ran 45960496863, 45960762506, 45960978175 and 45961174423 in turn). Check the run''s returned count before queuing the next.',array['migrate','apply','conductor','pitfall'],'proposed','docs/session_742_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyWillet (S741)','2026-11-27'),
('f-ela-committed-passes-live-older-s741','fact','Ten East Los Angeles records pass in committed files but sit live on older runs','S741: ten East Los Angeles records whose committed file is the reconcile 45176404274 sit live on older runs; eight pass in the committed files (35087, 35088, 35888, 37510, 38337, 41132, 43725, 45987), so the census counts them passed where the live table may not. Keep-better''s generic-heading test also refuses ''(Academic Plan E002456C)''.',array['program-requirements','east-los-angeles','census','follow-up'],'proposed','docs/session_742_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyWillet (S741)','2026-11-27'),
('f-keep-better-major-equal-rank-s741','fact','Keep-better ranks an incomplete re-read with the major equal above a filed unequal only where the filed major is not equal','S741: keep-better ranks an ''incomplete, major equal'' re-read above a filed ''unequal'' (210 such records statewide) only where the filed record''s own major is not equal. Otherwise a re-read that lost the GE units would beat a filed record holding them: 79 filed records at 27 colleges are unequal at the degree with the major equal, and all keep their filed record.',array['program-requirements','keep-better','reread','recall'],'proposed','docs/session_742_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyWillet (S741)','2026-11-27')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

